 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Salt seasons the potato, glucose helps browning and baking soda encourages a rougher surface.</li><li>Weigh the soda carefully: too much can make the potatoes break apart or taste alkaline.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "What the brine does"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>For this batch use <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 g</span> glucose syrup or <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"1.25\" data-s=\"0\">1.25 g</span> granulated sugar</b>, not both.</li><li>The substitution follows ChefSteps’ stated ratio.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Sugar is not a 1:1 substitute"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The 25-minute cook and first fry are guides for these thick batons.</li><li>Check tenderness before draining.</li><li>Thin fries need a different schedule; do not run them through this one unchanged.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Different potato or thickness?"
  }
 ],
